<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Live-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit). A build seat on lane b1-lift. Edit ONE file: packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/shore-writes.e2e.test.ts (and, only if the same helper is copied verbatim there, the sibling e2e files that copy it; list them, change none of their other lines). Do not commit.

THE FAULT (measured by Mount-Warden, /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/resume.md "Mount-Warden step"): waitForLivePage (~:200-221) waits a fixed 20000 ms TOTAL for a #phases .phase reading `live`, then for data-lar-shown="mirror" and a nonempty .lar-mirror pane. A founding boot in CI takes 21.6-27.2 s on green runs and progresses phase by phase (boot, repo-open, catalog-ready, bootstrap-kept, island-ready, corpus-ready, wiki-ready, vessel-ready, tw5-booted, live); every red cut it at 20.2 s at a different phase. No await hangs.

THE CURE (the house law from 31180ff9d slot-wake: the timer bounds SILENCE alone, never progress): the live wait fails only when no NEW #phases entry arrives for a silence window (keep 20 s as that window), and reads each new phase as progress that restarts the window; a hard ceiling stays as a backstop (60 s, the slot-wait cap's precedent) so a looping boot still reads red. The mirror wait after `live` keeps its own window. On failure the message still names the phases seen and the faults, and names which wait failed (silence after phase X, or the ceiling). No sleep, no retry loop, no wider single budget.
A unit-level pin where it fits without a browser: if the helper can take its clock and phase reader as parameters, add a plain node test beside it (packages/lararium-web/tests/live-wait.test.ts) that drives fake phases: steady progress past 20 s total passes (the red today); 20 s of silence after vessel-ready fails naming vessel-ready (control); progress past the 60 s ceiling fails naming the ceiling. If parameterizing would reach product code, skip the unit pin and say so.
Run that one node test file only (no browser, no e2e). Write out.md with the diff summary and the test tally.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

